  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 330 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nThe trough that has brought precipitation to the region \novernight into this morning (and a few lingering pockets of \ndrizzle in north central MN) is transitioning to the north, \nwhile the next shortwave trough that will bring rain chances \nWednesday is centered over Oregon upstream. After the next wave \npasses Wednesday a large upper low and persistent trough \npattern is shown to remain entrenched upstream over the Pacific\nNorthwest, with a general SW flow pattern across the central \nRockies towards the Northern Plains. Our immediate region will \ntend to be under broader ridging within this split-southwest \nflow pattern initially keeping more active tracks and rain \nchances out of the region. However as the more active SW flow \npattern builds east towards the weekend there are general rain \nchances which increase as the larger upper low/trough finally \nmoves east of the Rockies into early next week. Current \nconsensus keeps this to the south, however there is still a \nbroad precipitation signal with this pattern change. Due to \nabove average air mass remain in place there continues to be a \nsignal/trend towards only rain.\n\n...Rain on Wednesday...\n\nThe shortwave trough over Oregon quickly progresses across\nRockies and into the Northern Plains overnight tonight into \nWednesday morning and increasing forcing for ascent, moisture \nreturn, and some instability should support increasing rain \ncoverage particularly in MN head of an associated frontal zone. \nThere may be enough instability for some thunderstorm activity \nacross west central MN which could contribute to localized \nhigher rain totals. Strong/severe storms are not anticipated \nthis far north with any potential for higher instability farther\nsouth. General totals will be lighter for most areas with probs\nfor 0.1\" and 0.25\" high east of the RRV but probability in \nNBM/HREF for 0.5\" lower (20-30% in our far east) and likely \ndependent on convective activity.",
